course: dictionary
lesson: 12663
title: Spreading out and fading away
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dissipation is a noun, and it comes from the verb «dissipate». When something dissipates, it slowly spreads out and gets lost until it has gone. Think of a puddle drying in the sun, or a cloud melting away in the blue sky.
explain: Scientists use this word a lot. «Some energy is dissipated as heat and sound when a machine runs.» The energy does not vanish, but it spreads out into the air and cannot be used again in the same way. That is why no machine is perfectly efficient.
explain: The word can also mean wasting things. «Too much dissipation of money left him with none for food.» Here, money, time or effort is spent carelessly, and it disappears without doing any good. Use the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Dissipation means the slow spreading out and loss of something, such as energy, heat or a cloud.
fact: «Dissipate» is the verb: «The fog began to dissipate as the sun came up.»
fact: Heat dissipation is when heat spreads out into the air around it.
fact: Dissipation can also mean wasting money, time or effort.
fact: In old-fashioned stories, «dissipation» describes a wild life of too much drinking and pleasure, and it is used to show disapproval.
exercise: «The fog began to dissipate as the sun came up.» What does dissipate mean here? | *Slowly fade away | Grow thicker and darker | Turn into rain | Freeze solid
exercise: In science, «some energy is dissipated as heat and sound». What does this tell you? | Energy turns into water | Sound makes the energy grow bigger | *Some energy spreads out and is lost | All energy is kept safe inside the machine
exercise: Which sentence uses dissipation to mean wasting money? | «The fog dissipated slowly over the lake.» | *«He dissipated his whole week's pocket money in one afternoon.» | «The heat dissipated into the cold room.» | «The clouds dissipated before lunch.»
test: In an old story, «He lived a life of dissipation, drinking and partying every night.» What does dissipation mean? | *Wild, wasteful living with too much drinking and pleasure | Kind help for people in need | Hard work on a busy farm | Quiet study in a library
test: Which word is closest in meaning to dissipate when a cloud disappears? | Shout | Freeze | *Fade | Gather
exam: The mist began to dissipate on the hill, so what happened to it? | It froze into ice on the path | It turned into snow on the grass | It became thicker and whiter | *It slowly faded away into the air
